<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">12052026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Washington is openly weighing a return to combat against Iran, and the conversation has moved past airstrikes.</s> <s>Trump and Netanyahu have floated, on the record, a ground operation to seize the uranium for roughly twelve warheads still sitting in the Isfahan ruins, after Tehran's peace letter dropped its nuclear pledge.</s> <s>The administration is split between a hawks' camp pushing strikes and a diplomacy track, and a final decision, officials say, is days away.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Britain's quietly let nearly two hundred sanctioned Russian shadow-fleet tankers pass through its waters without a single boarding.</s> <s>Prime Minister Starmer announced in March that the armed forces could intercept these vessels, yet two hundred and thirty-eight passages have since gone unchallenged, and the Ministry of Defence has produced no evidence of disruption.</s> <s>A former Royal Navy officer told the BBC the gap exposes how thin Western sanctions enforcement has become once the cameras move on.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Moscow, the veteran Vadim Sharipov was sent home from the front with a metal rod where his arm used to be.</s> <s>Russia's state-led prosthetics sector is scaling fast on the Ukraine war's amputees, churning out Soviet-era generic devices that still depend on Western components, while the disability entitlement system tightens around the men who need custom fittings.</s> <s>Another Bakhmut veteran has now appealed directly to Putin, putting the political economy of war injury on the Kremlin's own desk.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In the West Bank, the UN has confirmed forty thousand Palestinians displaced since January of last year through settler raids and demolitions in Area C.</s> <s>Last week alone, forty-two people, twelve of them children, lost their homes, and the UN says the pattern violates the international prohibition on forced transfer under occupation.</s> <s>This is a parallel displacement to Gaza, carried out without a single named operation, and Europe's recent settler sanctions have not slowed it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's prime minister has extended a nationwide austerity decree until the thirteenth of June, with sixty percent of the government fleet now grounded.</s> <s>Sharif's banned ministerial travel, cut state offices to a four-day week, and pushed conservation orders as the Hormuz blockade stretches the oil shock into the bones of state logistics.</s> <s>The federal budget lands in early June, and households are now learning that the Iran war reaches them as a state-imposed conservation regime, six weeks at a time.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Kyiv's anti-corruption agencies have charged Andriy Yermak, the man who ran Zelensky's office for the entire war, with organising the laundering of ten and a half million dollars through an elite housing complex.</s> <s>Yermak denies owning property in the development, and the presidential office says it'll cooperate.</s> <s>It's the first real test of whether wartime executive power in Ukraine has any internal check at all.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>JPMorgan is now telling clients that even if the Strait of Hormuz reopens tomorrow, Brent crude will average ninety-seven dollars across the rest of the year.</s> <s>Aramco's chief, Amin Nasser, warns the bottleneck has simply migrated, from the waterway itself to tanker charters, insurance markets, and refinery queues that take months to clear.</s> <s>A diplomatic win, in other words, still leaves importers paying war-time prices well into next year.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Damascus, the European Union has ended a fourteen-year suspension of Syrian trade on the same day the United Arab Emirates flew in its first post-Assad business delegation.</s> <s>Syria's also pursuing its first sovereign credit rating, the precondition for serious capital flows.</s> <s>The World Bank prices Syrian reconstruction at two hundred and sixteen billion dollars, and the queue to underwrite it is now forming.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Seventeen American chief executives, including the heads of Apple, Tesla, Boeing, and Goldman Sachs, are boarding Trump's flight to Beijing this week.</s> <s>The delegation represents the sectors most exposed to the tariff regime, and the visit follows a preliminary trade deal reached only last week.</s> <s>It's the first US presidential trip to China of this term, and Xi will host the meetings from Wednesday through Friday.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>An Andean court has ruled that Colombia did not breach regional trade law when it broke the patent on the HIV drug dolutegravir.</s> <s>Bogotá issued the compulsory licence on public-health grounds, and the ruling now hands Bolivia, Ecuador, and Peru a tested legal template for doing the same.</s> <s>Pharmaceutical companies operating across the Andes have just lost a layer of protection they'd long assumed was unshakeable.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Geologists working Zambia's geothermal springs have found helium isotope ratios that can only be explained one way... the country's crust has cracked through to the mantle beneath it.</s> <s>That's the chemical signature of a new continental rift forming inside Africa, a process that, on geological timescales, eventually splits a plate.</s> <s>The same weak crust that may one day tear apart is also what makes Zambia's geothermal energy potential exceptional today.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Ghana's Tamale Metropolis, one in every five paediatric nurses now shows severe daytime sleepiness after night shifts.</s> <s>A study of one hundred and seventy-five nurses identifies shift-scheduling ratios, not workload or pay, as the strongest predictor of physiological harm.</s> <s>Researchers have asked Ghana's Health Service to redesign rotations, an intervention that costs nothing and protects both the nurses and the children in their wards.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nigeria's recorded one hundred and ninety Lassa fever deaths so far this year, and the case fatality rate has climbed to twenty-five percent, up from nineteen the year before.</s> <s>The country's disease-control agency blames late presentation at hospital, since the antiviral ribavirin works only when given early.</s> <s>Eighty-four percent of cases sit in just five states, which means the response problem is sharply geographic and entirely solvable.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Apple's quietly switched on end-to-end encryption for Rich Communication Services messages between iPhones and Android phones on Monday.</s> <s>The lock icon arrives by default in iOS twenty-six point five, and for the first time, carriers, governments, and the platforms themselves cannot read cross-platform texts in transit.</s> <s>It's the largest expansion of consumer encryption in years, and it happened without a single press conference.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Google's Threat Intelligence Group says criminals have now deployed a working zero-day exploit built by AI.</s> <s>The model identified an authentication flaw in an unnamed platform, wrote the exploit, and reached attackers before Google could patch.</s> <s>Google warns that for every AI-traced zero-day they catch, many more pass unattributed, which means the defenders' visibility into this new attack class is already partial.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Brazil's antitrust authority has opened a formal probe into Google's AI Overviews, the summary box that strips traffic from the news publishers whose articles it's built on.</s> <s>Investigators must now draw a line between traditional search snippets and AI summaries that send users nowhere.</s> <s>Where Brasília lands will shape how every other antitrust regulator in the Global South frames the same question.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>